  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1133 PM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nUpper level ridging over southern California Sunday expands east \nover much of the desert SW Monday as the upper low over Mexico \nshifts northeast over Texas. High temperatures across the area \nincrease a few degrees compared to Sunday with light winds and \nmostly sunny skies continuing. The weak ridge overhead breaks down \nTuesday as a trough moves southeast across the northern and central \nRockies and Great Plains. No noticeable changes in the sensible \nweather compared to Monday. Upper level ridging over the Great Basin \nand troughing over the Great Plains helps sends a weak backdoor \nfront through eastern NM Wednesday morning resulting in light north \nwinds. The upper ridge slides east closer to the state Thursday \nbefore moving overhead Friday allowing the tranquil November weather \nto continue! High clouds move in from the west late in the day \nFriday as a storm system moves into the Pacific coast. High \ntemperatures next week will be near to slightly above average, while \nlow temperatures will be slightly to well above average for mid \nNovember.",
